---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons search -h <==
Find addons by name in the catalog, WoWInterface, Tukui and GitHub

Usage: omaddons search [OPTIONS] <QUERY>...
Aliases: find

Arguments:
  <QUERY>...  What to look for: words of the addon's name, folders, author or description

Options:
      --source <SOURCE>  Consult only this source (repeatable): catalog, wowi, tukui or github
      --limit <LIMIT>    Most results to list (default 20, at most 50)
      --refresh          Fetch the WoWInterface index and the Tukui list now, even inside their
                         windows

Examples:
  omaddons search damage meter -t retail    every source at once, judged for retail
  omaddons search questie --source catalog  the built-in catalog only

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons search --help <==
Find addons by name in the catalog, WoWInterface, Tukui and GitHub

Usage: omaddons search [OPTIONS] <QUERY>...
Aliases: find

Arguments:
  <QUERY>...
          What to look for: words of the addon's name, folders, author or description

Options:
      --source <SOURCE>
          Consult only this source (repeatable): catalog, wowi, tukui or github

      --limit <LIMIT>
          Most results to list (default 20, at most 50)

      --refresh
          Fetch the WoWInterface index and the Tukui list now, even inside their windows

Examples:
  omaddons search details           the catalog, WoWInterface, Tukui and GitHub at once
  omaddons find elvui --source tukui
  omaddons search bags --offline    what this machine already knows

Only GitHub's search receives the query; the catalog, the WoWInterface index and
the Tukui list are searched on this machine. Compatibility per client is a hint:
install verifies each addon's TOC.

See also: install, info

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the
                         Classic Era client), family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every
                         client) [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change
                         nothing)
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by
                         commands that change nothing)
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
